{"_id":"68a7363c8ec3d8323af1f087","nodeId":"BJ4fQvagTO0B5UtXblyx8","roadmapSlug":"sql","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:40.099Z","description":"# DATEPART\n\n`DATEPART` is a useful function in SQL that allows you to extract a specific part of a date or time field. You can use it to get the year, quarter, month, day of the year, day, week, weekday, hour, minute, second, or millisecond from any date or time expression.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"SQL DATEPART","url":"https://hightouch.com/sql-dictionary/sql-datepart","_id":"69bba6b933a0ad7a57afe70a"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-19T07:33:13.508Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d0416838","title":"DataCamp - SQL Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/ZVeXng"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d04167c7","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/sql/content/BJ4fQvagTO0B5UtXblyx8.md"}